    date "2020-11-20T03:05:58Z"
    title "Limited Growing Space? Use this Strategy to Maximize Yields! | Urban Gardening with Guten Yardening"
    description "Limited Growing Space? Use this Strategy to Maximize Yields! | Urban Gardening with Guten Yardening&#10;&#10;We have a limited amount of urban yardening space, and this means that we often have to be agressive in our planning succession planting.  The container we show you today is no exception to this rule.  &#10;&#10;In one food safe plastic 50 gallon container (cut long ways) an area of just over 5 square feet, we were able to grow radishes, potatoes, and carrots this season, for a total harvest nearing 15 lbs.  That is the equivalent of almost three pounds of food per square food, which makes this yield an important piece of our journey toward food freedom.&#10;&#10;When we consider the length of our growing season, we have to keep in mind that some of the vegetables we want to plant do better in the cool of the beginning or end of the growing season, and some prefer the heat of the middle of the season, and we plan and plant accordingly.&#10;&#10;Consider this intentional succession planting as a part of your yardening or gardening practices in the seasons to come, and you won't regret the decision at all.&#10;&#10;Thank you for watching!&#10;&#10;We hope you enjoy this video!  Thank you for watching!&#10;Shop With Us: https://gutenyardening.wixsite.com/website&#10;If you like my hat, you can get it here: https://amzn.to/3nmiYQl&#10;&#10;Follow us on twitter: https://twitter.com/GutenYardening&#10;And on instagram: https://www.instagram.com/gutenyardening&#10;&#10;Theme Song: Country Cue 1 by Audionautix is licensed under a Creative Commons Attribution license (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/...)&#10;Artist: http://audionautix.com/&#10;&#10;#successionplanting #potatoes #radishes #carrots #urbangardening"
    channeltitle "Guten Yardening"
