    id 71
    label "L7yGqDOUKwc"
    step 0
    date "2022-03-04T12:15:15Z"
    title "[Filipino W/ English Subs] Intro To Urban Gardening For Sustainable Living + Start Backyard Farming"
    description "Can we really create an organic mini farm in our backyard?  Can we make an organic farm out of a small space?  Watch this vlog to know if this is possible, and know how. &#10;&#10;#MylaCazVlogs&#10;#sustainablefarming&#10;#backyardgardening  &#10;#CanWeTurnBackyardGardeningIntoASustainableFarming&#10;#organic &#10;#organicfarming &#10;#TipsOnOrganicFarming&#10;#TipsOnHowToPlantSeeds&#10;#TipsOnBackyardGardening&#10;#waterpropagation &#10;#waterplants &#10;#pothos &#10;#pothosvarieties &#10;#philodendron &#10;#peperomiavarieties&#10;#peperomia &#10;#moringa &#10;#guyabano &#10;#papaya &#10;#banana &#10;#CissusVine&#10;#cissus&#10;#indoorplants &#10;#naturalairpurifiers&#10;#freerangechickenfarming &#10;#freerangechickens&#10;#fermentedchickenmanure&#10;#compost &#10;#composting&#10;#turmerictea&#10;#probiotics&#10;#lgv30 &#10;#lgphone &#10;&#10;&#10;WHAT IS A CISSUS DISCOLOR PLANT?&#10;&#10;Cissus discolor&#160;is the botanical name for a lovely tropical vine known as the rex begonia vine or the tapestry vine. Through this plant is completely unrelated to actual rex begonias, the leaves are multi-colored and have an appearance very similar to a rex begonia, hence the common name.&#10;&#10;A native of Southeast Asia, including Java and Cambodia, this vining plant is more closely related to a grape plant than it is to a begonia (it&#8217;s in the&#160;Vitaceae&#160;family). The genus&#160;Cissus&#160;has two other popular species in it:&#160;C.&#160;rhombifolia, a popular houseplant known as grape ivy, and&#160;C. quadrangularis, a medicinal plant with a thick stem. There are several hundred additional species within the genus&#160;Cissus, but most are not regularly cultivated by gardeners.&#10;&#10;*How do you care for a CISSUS plant?*&#10;&#10;Cissus houseplants prefer consistently damp soil, but let the top half of the soil dry out before watering. You can cut back on watering during the winter when the plant is not actively growing.&#10;&#10;&#10;DO INDOOR PLANTS REALLY SERVE AS NATURAL AIR PURIFIERS?&#10;&#10;Plants are indispensable to human life. Through photosynthesis, they convert the carbon dioxide we exhale into fresh oxygen, and they can also remove toxins from the air we breathe.&#10;&#10;One&#160;famous NASA experiment, published in 1989, found that indoor plants can scrub the air of cancer-causing volatile organic compounds like formaldehyde and benzene. (Those NASA researchers were looking for ways to effectively detoxify the air of space station environments.) Later&#160;research&#160;has found that soil microorganisms in potted plants also play a part in cleaning indoor air.&#10;&#10;&#10;_________________________________________&#10;&#10;&#128077;Massive thanks BuGuMi for the lovely tracks which I used in this video vlog.&#128077;&#10;__________________________________________&#10;&#10;WHERE I PURCHASED PLANTS AND GOT MY FREEBIES: &#10;&#10;Special thanks to #GerlynCastilloFlowerAndGardenShop &#10;Located in Sitio Langhaya, Marcos Hi-way, Antipolo City  (Rizal)&#10;___________________________________________&#10;&#10;Connect With Me :&#10;&#10;FACEBOOK: Myla Caz&#10;FACEBOOK PAGE:  MYLA CAZ VLOGS&#10;INSTAGRAM: mylacastro8888&#10;&#10;___________________________________________&#10;&#10;For business and collaborations, kindly email me at: mylacazvlogs@gmail.com&#10;&#10;___________________________________________&#10;&#10;&#10;PHONE USED IN THIS VLOG&#10;&#10;LGV30"
    channeltitle "Myla Caz"
    channelid "UCuYtjQ2mbbGTaS-xvpCXzxA"
