    id 117
    label "WDcdTPyC5g4"
    step 0
    date "2015-10-30T15:53:16Z"
    title "Grow: An Urban Gardening Symposium"
    description "Manhattan is home to an array of urban plots, hydroponic farms, greenhouses, and more than 170 community gardens. This urban agriculture yields tremendous benefits for our neighborhoods, our economy, and the environment: it teaches valuable skills and sustainably produces fresh, healthy, locally-grown food.&#10;&#10;On October 14, 2015, Borough President Brewer hosted &#34;Grow: Urban Garden Symposium,&#34; to connect community members with urban agriculture experts and leaders. Through a series of panel discussions and an industry fair featuring more than fifteen exhibitors, participants learned how to expand their programs, or start a garden or farm of their own. &#10;&#10;The primary challenge to urban agriculture in Manhattan is one of limited, expensive space. Borough President Brewer hopes that by providing access to finding and resources, New Yorkers will be better able to pursue alternative gardening options and make Manhattan a greener, healthier borough. &#10;&#10;To that end, she has committed $1 million in capital grants for Manhattan public schools to invest in urban agriculture programs. She also administers a grant program to spur composting programs in community gardens, in partnership with the Manhattan Solid Waste Advisory Board and the Citizen's Committee for New York City. &#10;&#10;Learn more about what I've been doing and how you can get involved: http://manhattanbp.nyc.gov/urbangardens"
    channeltitle "Gale A. Brewer, Manhattan Borough President"
    channelid "UCIl8qNC8S905t58m43SH0XA"
