    step 0
    date "2021-07-29T18:30:55Z"
    title "LAMP Presents - Urban Gardening"
    description "The LAMP Urban Garden Internship Program is an income-qualifying program that combines leadership skill development with learning conventional gardening and hydroponics for youth aged 18-24 currently living in low-income households.&#10;&#10;The Leadership ARTS Mentoring Program (LAMP) aims to inspire and empower participants as they create personal and career growth plans to enable self-sustainability, overcome personal barriers and contribute positively to their families and communities.&#10;&#10;LAMP builds leadership skills in combination with creative disciplines in areas such as:&#10;        &#8226;    Film/TV Production&#10;        &#8226;    Graphic Design&#10;        &#8226;    Music Production&#10;        &#8226;    Photography&#10;        &#8226;    Urban Gardening and Hydroponics&#10;&#10;Why the arts? Studies show that at-risk youth who have access to the arts have better academic outcomes, higher career goals and are more civically engaged.&#10;&#10;For more information, call (562) 216-4645.&#10;https://lbcap.org/youth-lamp/"
    channeltitle "PADNETtv"
