    id 259
    label "ZG8rITUrZf8"
    step 0
    date "2021-04-09T19:10:23Z"
    title "Urban Gardening in Central Texas - April 2021 Garden Tour"
    description "Greetings fellow gardeners! This video is a tour of my backyard and front yard garden beds in Austin Texas. I made this video to share my experience of becoming a home owner and urban gardening in central Texas (Zone 8B). I bought my home in Feb 2020, and before then, I wasn't into gardening, but after moving in, gardening has become one of my favorite hobbies!&#10;&#10;I'm working with a smaller backyard, and a smaller lot in general. My home is on a 4400 square foot lot, and my backyard is 40'x16' which is 640 square feet. In my backyard, i've built an in-ground bed, where I'm growing peaches, cabbage, cauliflower, celery, strawberries, habaneros, cilantro, and basil. I've also got a circular raised bed that I built with limestone, which contains my larger peach tree, bluebonnets, and cucumber plants.&#10;&#10;In my front yard I'm growing wildflowers and an assortment of fruits and vegetables including olives, apples, figs, tomatoes, jalape&#241;os, habaneros, peas, a pineapple, a potted avocado tree, sweet potatoes, green onions, and more things on the way every day.&#10;&#10;Gardening in Austin Texas is super fun! Working with smaller urban spaces like mine can be difficult, but its rewarding, and I've had success with all kinds of fruits and veggies.&#10;&#10;Video Chapter Timestamps -&#10;0:00&#8203; Intro&#10;2:08&#8203; Backyard Garden Bed&#10;3:15&#8203; Winter Garden Bed Update&#10;5:22&#8203; Growing Strawberries&#10;9:30&#8203; Growing Peaches&#10;13:46 Front Yard Garden&#10;&#10;Thanks again for watching Austin Texas Gardening!&#10;&#10;#AustinTexas&#8203; #Gardening #GardenTour&#8203; #HowTo&#8203; #BackyardOrchard #Texas&#8203;&#8203; #Vegetable&#8203; #Garden&#8203;&#8203; #Organic&#8203;&#8203; #Gardener #SpringGarden"
    channeltitle "Austin Texas Gardening"
    channelid "UCP22Pv-8_bwXMU0gOkOVTTA"
