    id 451
    label "m2aZys2PBXY"
    step 0
    date "2019-05-12T15:44:24Z"
    title "How to Plant and Take Care of Cassava - Southwest Florida Urban Gardening"
    description "It's very easy to grow cassava from cuttings.  You may place a cutting vertically or 15 degree in the ground.  It doesn't require much water.&#10;&#10;Cassava (manihot esculenta) is also know as yuca, or tapioca.  It is a staple root crop that you can grow very easily in tropical region such as Florida.  It is a beautiful and delicious plant; its leaves are also edible.&#10;&#10;Cassava root  is starchy and used as food around the world especially in tropical countries.  Fresh cassava tastes very good, better than potatoes, but as good as yams.  You can eat it steamed or cooked in a dessert."
    channeltitle "2HCOMBO"
